      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely right that the primary driver of automation is often cost reduction through workforce restructuring rather than job creation. To prevent this scenario while still saving margins, many startups balance this by automating repetitive tasks instead of replacing entire roles, which allows human employees to focus on higher-value responsibilities. Instead of cutting teams, you can reframe these changes as \"role transformation\" initiatives where you invest in upskilling existing staff for hands-on projects, thereby maintaining morale even as overhead drops.",
