      "content": "i mean, upskilling sounds nice on paper, but it's expensive and slow. if a competitor just fires half their staff and uses ai to do the same work for a fraction of the cost, they're gonna crush me in the market. at some point, isn't it just more logical to accept that human labor is becoming a liability in a high-efficiency economy?",
